{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/WolfRiccardo/status/2118143241119740039","id":"2118143241119740039","text":"I created these with the new ChatGPT Images 2.6.\n\nA lot of people were quick to criticize ChatGPT Images 2.6, but I've been testing it for a few weeks now, and I've noticed significant improvements in several areas.\n\nMy tests mainly focus on cinematic visuals and photorealism, and there are many noticeable differences compared to 2.5.\n\nI started testing GIF generation about a month ago, and unfortunately, it's still pretty bad. I haven't seen any improvements over the past month. GIFs still struggle with consistency.\n\nHowever, image generation has improved significantly. It's more consistent, more realistic, and faster.\n\nAnd here's the interesting part: I believe many of the things you dislike about ChatGPT Images 2.6 will be addressed once the new Nano Banana Pro is released.\n\nChatGPT Images 3.0 is going to surprise all of you.","raw_text":{"text":"I created these with the new ChatGPT Images 2.6.\n\nA lot of people were quick to criticize ChatGPT Images 2.6, but I've been testing it for a few weeks now, and I've noticed significant improvements in several areas.\n\nMy tests mainly focus on cinematic visuals and photorealism, and there are many noticeable differences compared to 2.5.\n\nI started testing GIF generation about a month ago, and unfortunately, it's still pretty bad. I haven't seen any improvements over the past month. GIFs still struggle with consistency.\n\nHowever, image generation has improved significantly. It's more consistent, more realistic, and faster.\n\nAnd here's the interesting part: I believe many of the things you dislike about ChatGPT Images 2.6 will be addressed once the new Nano Banana Pro is released.\n\nChatGPT Images 3.0 is going to surprise all of you.","display_text_range":[0,840],"facets":[{"type":"media","indices":[278,301],"id":"2118142997808209920","display":"pic.x.com/nThLP4Esuw","ori